{"id":"e38848b6-c9aa-43e3-8391-f7e3eb157fb6","object":"chat.completion","created":1785034598,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"import json\\n\\ndef solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    retained = set(n['id'] for n in nodes if not n['removable'])\\n    parent_of = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        parent_of[n['id']] = n['parent']\\n    def add_ancestors(node_id):\\n        while node_id is not None and node_id not in retained:\\n            retained.add(node_id)\\n            node_id = parent_of.get(node_id)\\n    for sym in required_symbols:\\n        if any(node_map[nid]['symbol'] == sym for nid in retained):\\n            continue\\n        candidates = [n for n in nodes if n['symbol'] == sym and n['removable']]\\n        if not candidates:\\n            candidates = [n for n in nodes if n['symbol'] == sym]\\n        best = max(candidates, key=lambda x: (x['utility'], x['id']))\\n        add_ancestors(best['id'])\\n    all_ids = set(n['id'] for n in nodes)\\n    removed = sorted(all_ids - retained)\\n    retained_list = sorted(retained)\\n    return {'removed_node_ids': removed, 'retained_node_ids': retained_list}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to write a Python solve(case) function that takes the payload (which has nodes list and required_symbols list) and returns a JSON object with removed_node_ids and retained_node_ids. The task is about pruning a tree: given nodes with id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility. We need to decide which nodes to remove and which to retain, presumably to satisfy required_symbols while maximizing something? But the problem description is not fully given; we only see the public fixtures. We must infer the algorithm from the examples? The task is \"SE-PE-01\" and the registry \"B\". The fixture shows three cases with similar structure. All